From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcrypt: the CNG configuration API (contexts, functions, providers)

- BCryptCreateContext/DeleteContext/ConfigureContext/QueryContextConfiguration/
  EnumContexts, BCryptAdd/RemoveContextFunction, EnumContextFunctions,
  Configure/QueryContextFunctionConfiguration, Add/RemoveContextFunctionProvider,
  EnumContextFunctionProviders, Set/QueryContextFunctionProperty,
  BCryptRegisterProvider/UnregisterProvider/QueryProviderRegistration,
  BCryptEnumRegisteredProviders and BCryptEnumProviders (23 functions) were
  stubs: some answered success and kept nothing, the rest were missing or
  returned STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED. They are now a real store (dlls/bcrypt/
  config.c), kept in memory for the process, shaped like the registry
  configuration Windows keeps: local and domain tables of named contexts, an
  ordered function list per interface, an ordered provider list and named
  properties per function, and provider registrations.
- The Default context and the "Microsoft Primitive Provider" are seeded from
  BCryptEnumAlgorithms, so they cannot disagree with it; an SSL context exists
  and is empty. Names are caseless. Positions work (0 is the top,
  CRYPT_PRIORITY_BOTTOM appends). Results are single allocations that
  BCryptFreeBuffer frees, or fill a caller buffer (STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL with
  the size needed). Registrations are deep copied; QueryProviderRegistration
  filters by mode and interface.
- include/bcrypt.h gets the structures and constants these need.
- bcrypt test: BCryptEnumContextFunctions(SSL, NCRYPT_SCHANNEL_INTERFACE) no
  longer todo_wine.

Gate: test/bcryptconfig-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/bcryptconfig-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_BCCFG_ORDER/NOSEED/FILTER/CASE (bcrypt/config.c).
